# The old area formats: #MOBOLD and #OBJOLD (db.c load_old_mob, load_old_obj) and their conversion (db2.c
# convert_mobile, convert_objects, convert_object), with tools/fixtures/files/oldformat.are loaded first (its
# area.lst is area-oldformat.lst), so its first 'O' reset comes before any mob's.
# - the boot: convert_mobile draws a damage type for each old mob as it loads (the rng line), and every prototype is
#   new-format by the end (memory's "new format" counts)
# - stat mob on each old mob: its race from the first keyword (a quoted 'giant troll' is no race, so human blanks),
#   dice, armour and wealth made up from the level, positions below sleeping made standing; look shows the
#   first letters the loader upper-cases (a long description and a description) and lower-cases (a short one)
# - stat obj on each old object: its level from the mob or container its resets put it with (shop goods have a floor
#   by type), its cost and values from the level, spell slots looked up, a two-handed sword's flag
# - the bread's 'P' reset has no room under its limit (0), so stat obj finds none until @obj makes one
# - list in the old smith's shop: the prices come from the made-up costs
@place oldformat.are oldformat.are
@place area-oldformat.lst area.lst
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
holylight
memory
goto 31000
look
look oldguard
stat mob oldguard
stat mob oldsage
stat mob oldbrute
stat mob oldchild
stat obj oldsword
stat obj oldmail
stat obj oldpill
stat obj oldidol
stat obj oldchest
stat obj oldbread
stat obj oldcoins
stat obj oldlamp
stat obj oldgem
stat obj oldclub
stat obj oldbone
@obj 31008 31000
stat obj oldbread
goto 31001
stat mob oldsmith
stat obj oldpotion
stat obj oldscroll
stat obj oldwand
stat obj oldstaff
list
@state
